00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:03.200
Film Courage: Do you consider yourself an artist?

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.400
Chris Gore, Founder/Owner of&nbsp;
FilmThreat/Author/Filmmaker: Oh wow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:12.720
do I consider myself an artist. I would say&nbsp;
yes in the sense that I try to do something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:20.400
creative every day and I try to live what I would&nbsp;
describe as a creative life. I drove to your place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.520
here in my car and most people that buy a car&nbsp;
they just okay they get their car and that's it. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:36.160
have no allegiance to Toyota and I turned&nbsp;
my car into a Batmobile where I have Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.520
stickers in certain places on the hubcaps on&nbsp;
all the interior in the console I covered up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:50.000
the Toyota logo with a Batman logo and so I try to&nbsp;
like and if you ever come to my place everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.600
from the bookshelves is just something creatively&nbsp;
stimulating everywhere. I always have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:02.480
creative project I'm doing whether I'm modifying&nbsp;
something and then even with my website and film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.160
projects there's sort of a handmade feel to it so&nbsp;
I guess artists would be an all-encompassing thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.720
in that describes the way I live my life also&nbsp;
the way I like to write I don't I just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:21.200
if everyone's doing this thing I'm trying to do&nbsp;
I'm trying to go the other way or find another way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:27.040
or we've heard this line a million times I'm going&nbsp;
to try something different so I would say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.480
like artists would be a good all-encompassing&nbsp;
thing but I would never say that about myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.360
but I think in and live that way because I&nbsp;
tend to not accept the choices we're given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.840
and by that I mean one of the&nbsp;
things when I was in high school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.360
they try to see what your capacity is for&nbsp;
certain careers right and one of the questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.640
that puzzled a teacher of mine was why did you&nbsp;
