People [Author Stephen Covey] and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.040
I usually get like one or two nuggets of&nbsp;
like oh that's really good but you gotta like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:02.480
sift through that 60,000 words to get to that&nbsp;
like that you know a pot of gold of knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:09.120
but I began to realize that part of this is&nbsp;
about is about breaking down processes no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.840
writes a book or just makes a movie or writes&nbsp;
a screenplay it's breaking that process down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:20.240
into the smallest smallest task and then just&nbsp;
doing that task every day like anything and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:26.800
creating a habit and I think that scientifically&nbsp;
speaking they say that it takes about three weeks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:32.640
to instill a habit and I think that if you can&nbsp;
develop those good habits and just do a piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:40.240
even if it's a paragraph you're gonna have I mean&nbsp;
it boggles my mind when I see people who do these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.960
long Facebook posts or social media social media&nbsp;
posts and I look at that and I said if you took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:53.120
that energy and you put it into like a book&nbsp;
or a screenplay or some other piece of work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.200
and you just you would really have something I&nbsp;
feel like I feel like we're we're giving away our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:08.400
creativity to these social media companies and it&nbsp;
I i it's it's it's really disheartening to see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

